('p', 'Long runs start afresh at normalized (q,p,h)=(1,0,0.1). A full three-column QR calculation uses the analytic branch Jacobian in (q,p,log h). Its summed rates agree with independently accumulated log determinants within 9.1 x 10<super>-14</super>. No selected tail closes in the declared lag-1–512 test at tolerance 10<super>-9</super>; that is not proof of aperiodicity.'),
('p', 'Independent precision calculations evaluate all seven rational stages and import neither the production map nor its Jacobian. Two finite-separation directions in actual (q,p,h) are orthogonalized, with separations 10<super>-30</super> and 10<super>-40</super>. Each run uses 100,000 warm-up, 5,000 alignment and 100,000 measured steps in ten windows. Parameters and controller constants are exact lifts of the declared binary64 values.'),
('p', 'Unmodified SciPy 1.18.1 takes 400,000 steps from physical (q,p)=(1,0), atol=10<super>-6</super>, first h=0.1. After 100,000 warm-up and 10,000 tangent alignment, all 29 leading windows are positive for the four cases; all D335 second windows are positive too. One-step residuals stay below 9.4 x 10<super>-9</super>. Tangents describe the mathematical map on library states, not floating-point rounding.'),
