('p', 'The wide slice covers zeta<sub>0</sub> plus or minus 0.018; the narrow slice covers plus or minus 0.0005. Both grids and their 400,000-step observation protocol were fixed before execution. Each setting uses a fresh normalized (q,p,h)=(1,0,0.1), 100,000 warm-up and twenty measured windows. The exact base parameter is included in both slices as a duplicate control.'),
('p', 'The leading criterion requires every first-rate window above 0.001 and no tested numerical period. Two-positive requires every second window above zero as well. Sampled intervals containing these flags are not certified open hyperchaotic regions. Periodic and weak outcomes are retained; the wide-neighbor test already shows why structural stability must not be inferred from one striking portrait.'),
